# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 035 — supersedes gap-033
# Act: SIG*  (Signal aimed at Pattern)   Stance: Tracing   Site: Kind
#
# gap-033 refused this act for the "anomalous" kind specifically, for lack
# of a second independent instance. That gap is superseded, not deleted:
# turn-32 bound "anomalous" to signal-c's outlier (96.04 widths); turn-34
# binds it to signal-d's, independently generated (seed 101 vs. 83),
# opposite sign, different magnitude (62.49 widths) — the same kind of
# claim, not the same instance.
#
# Traced directly: both entities' signs read "anomalous," both computed by
# the identical mechanism (a ground built from the other 31 values,
# distance measured in aperture-widths), neither inferred from the other.
# noise-control's "ordinary" (-0.10 widths, turn-32) remains the negative
# control this kind's sign is checked against, same as the "absent"/
# "present" kind's own control — one control, reused legitimately across
# both kinds it was built the same way to serve.
#
# What this earns, precisely: "anomalous" is now a stable sign for THIS
# kind (present, far outside a ground built from its own series' other
# values), independently of "absent"/"present," which is a different kind
# at the same cell. Gap-033's own finding stands unmodified — the two
# kinds' recurrences were never the same claim, and this turn closes only
# the one it was missing.
#
# Earning argument: precondition is turn-34 (a second independent
# instance) and turn-32 (the first, plus the negative control). Refuted if
# the two anomalous instances disagreed in sign — checked, both read
# "anomalous."

:turn-35  eot:opens        :turn-34 .
:turn-35  eot:supersedes   :gap-033 .
:turn-35  eot:act          eot:SIG* .
:turn-35  eot:stance       "Tracing" .
:turn-35  eot:site         "Kind" .
:turn-35  eot:for_kind     "anomalous" .
:turn-35  eot:traces       :turn-32 .
:turn-35  eot:traces       :turn-34 .
:turn-35  eot:consistent   true .
:turn-35  eot:witnessed    true .
:turn-35  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
